      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Baryancistrus longipinnis (Kindle, 1895)</li><li>Synonyms: Hemiancistrus longipinnis, Parancistrus longipinnis</li><li>Type locality: Troceira on Rio Tocantins, Brazil.</li><li>Etymology: Greek, barys = heavy + Greek, agkistron = hook - essentially \"Heavy Ancistrus\". The specific epithet means \"long fins\".</li><li>IUCN Red List category: Not Evaluated</li></ul>"
